id: pm-todos-tnou
title: Packed acceptance reports a bare timeout without scenario or subprocess diagnostics
description: "Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-todos#165 (filed 2026-10-28, missed by the blind issue watch). scripts/accept-packed.ts on current main still throws only '<command> exceeded <deadline>ms and was terminated' in its ETIMEDOUT branch (line ~80): it drops the captured stdout/stderr and the scenario name, so a hung 'bun init -y' (observed once on release PR #164's Node 26 job, 2026-10-28) cannot be diagnosed — no scenario, no output, no environment hint. The releases themselves have since succeeded (v2026.10.29 through v2026.10.31 green), so this is the remaining diagnostic gap, not a release blocker: include the scenario name and captured output in timeout errors and fail closed with the scenario list when a scenario never starts."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,diagnostics,"gh:unbraind/pm-todos#165"
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:18:44.778Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T15:23:30.877Z"
author: pi-glm
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T15:12:19.018Z",codex-sol,"Issue 165 remains reproducible on main: the subprocess timeout branch drops captured output and scenario context, and receipts appear only after all scenarios succeed. Reuse this tagged item. Plan: deterministic real-process timeout regression in a non-git SDK tracker, shared bounded sanitized diagnostics for every subprocess, partial receipts and runtime context, unchanged five-minute production timeout and all six current scenarios. Historical Bun hang cause and repeatability remain unknown."
  "2026-11-06T15:15:59.004Z",codex-sol,"Failing-first proof: the original timeout behavior fails the real subprocess regression (0/1) because the diagnostic has no bun-current scenario. The corrected runner passes 5/5 targeted tests, including a real non-git SDK tracker, timeout termination, nonzero exit, missing executable, bounded privacy-preserving previews, exact matrix completion, and the actual entrypoint failure report. npm run build:test, npm run typecheck and npm run docstring pass; this repository has no separate lint script."
  "2026-11-06T15:18:02.757Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral reverts were run only in disposable copies. Reverting runPackedCommand to the original subprocess behavior fails 3/5 tests; replacing summarizePackedOutput with raw passthrough fails 4/5; removing packedMatrixReport completion enforcement fails 1/5; restoring the entrypoint throw-only failure path fails its focused test 1/1. All reverted implementations were discarded, and the fixed targeted suite passed again. Linked pm test run passed 5/5; automatic result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt. Tracker commands use the pinned CLI 2026.11.4; the public registry reports 2026.11.6, and dependencies remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T15:23:24.166Z",codex-sol,"The npm-only Bun probe guard also fails its focused entrypoint test on behavioral revert (0/1). Local targeted tests, typechecking, test compilation, docstrings, changelog verification, privacy review and append-only history checks pass. An additional isolated-HOME npm release:check run reached the unchanged full coverage suite but was deliberately stopped because of shared-host load; it is not passing full-gate evidence. Per the task, CI will run both complete npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds. The underlying historical Bun hang remains unexplained; this change fixes its demonstrated diagnostic gap and preserves every current consumer."
